1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,330
An apron.

2
00:00:01,680 --> 00:00:02,610
A hangar.

3
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:04,356
Two inspection drones.

4
00:00:04,706 --> 00:00:06,101
An aircraft taxiing.

5
00:00:06,451 --> 00:00:09,242
One drone slips behind the hangar.

6
00:00:09,592 --> 00:00:12,383
What should the screen say now?

7
00:00:13,383 --> 00:00:16,638
MoVi declares what it has not observed.

8
00:00:16,988 --> 00:00:20,709
For every tracked object, one of three
answers.

9
00:00:21,059 --> 00:00:22,455
I see it.

10
00:00:22,805 --> 00:00:27,456
I don't see it: here is where it can be.

11
00:00:27,806 --> 00:00:29,666
Or: I don't know.

12
00:00:30,016 --> 00:00:34,667
What it has not observed, it marks
unverified, never empty.

13
00:00:35,017 --> 00:00:39,669
A possible-presence warning stays on until
a sensor looks again.

14
00:00:40,669 --> 00:00:46,250
Radar, LiDAR, visible and thermal cameras,
and what aircraft and drones broadcast.

15
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:49,391
All simulated from public data sheets.

16
00:00:49,741 --> 00:00:53,927
Each sensor has blind spots, and MoVi
draws them.

17
00:00:56,669 --> 00:00:58,529
Fog, then heavy rain.

18
00:00:58,879 --> 00:01:03,960
By calculation, the cameras' reach
collapses, and MoVi declares it, per

19
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:04,461
sensor.

20
00:01:04,811 --> 00:01:08,066
Only the radar is left: no redundancy.

21
00:01:08,416 --> 00:01:14,623
If the radar also fails, a fault we
inject, reliability is lost: warnings

22
00:01:14,623 --> 00:01:16,323
would come too late.

23
00:01:17,669 --> 00:01:19,530
Two drones fly close.

24
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:22,671
Too close to separate: unresolved tracks.

25
00:01:23,021 --> 00:01:24,416
Then they touch.

26
00:01:24,766 --> 00:01:26,161
Event: contact, inferred.

27
00:01:26,511 --> 00:01:31,162
A possible-debris volume opens, and never
shrinks on its own.

28
00:01:31,512 --> 00:01:35,233
The operator is warned: a person is
underneath.

29
00:01:35,583 --> 00:01:38,374
The ground stays unverified until
inspected.

30
00:01:39,669 --> 00:01:44,320
An engine fails on the take-off run, with
a flash.

31
00:01:44,670 --> 00:01:48,856
The flash blinds the cameras: MoVi marks
them unreliable.

32
00:01:49,206 --> 00:01:53,857
In the model, the radar alone still sees
the aircraft.

33
00:01:54,207 --> 00:01:56,533
Behind the smoke: not observed.

34
00:01:56,883 --> 00:01:58,743
Downstream: possible debris, unverified.

35
00:01:59,743 --> 00:02:01,139
First, the limits.

36
00:02:01,489 --> 00:02:07,070
Everything you saw is simulated from
public data sheets: no physical sensor.

37
00:02:07,420 --> 00:02:10,211
Object classes are labelled by hand.

38
00:02:10,561 --> 00:02:15,677
[STATO-1] The full chain has not yet run
end to end.

39
00:02:16,027 --> 00:02:18,353
Total delay is not measured.

40
00:02:18,703 --> 00:02:22,889
What holds: written rules decide, not a
trained model.

41
00:02:23,239 --> 00:02:28,820
[CIFRA-V2] In simulation, hidden objects
left without a warning: [k] of [n].

42
00:02:29,820 --> 00:02:35,738
The core comes from our short-range
version: a person behind an obstacle, a

43
00:02:35,738 --> 00:02:38,657
depth camera, the same three answers.

44
00:02:40,820 --> 00:02:41,286
MoVi.

45
00:02:41,636 --> 00:02:45,356
Seen, not seen, unknown: declared for
every track.

46
00:02:45,706 --> 00:02:47,567
It observes and warns.

47
00:02:47,917 --> 00:02:50,243
No output is a command.

48
00:02:50,593 --> 00:02:51,523
By SDMs.
